  "notes": "Pulau School in Adamstown, the islands' only school, teaches a curriculum based on The New Zealand Curriculum with New Zealand-registered teachers, and reports on Years 1–10; schooling is compulsory from 5 to 16 (GPI education policy). Year levels and ages follow New Zealand, where children start school at five, primary is Years 1–8 and secondary Years 9–13. Older students usually continue secondary school in New Zealand or by correspondence."
